      \field{abstract}{We investigate the three-dimensional Hubbard model and show that paramagnon exchange near a spin-density-wave instability gives rise to a strong singlet 𝑑-wave pairing interaction. For a cubic band the singlet (𝑑𝑥2−𝑦2 and 𝑑3⁢𝑧2−𝑟2) channels are enhanced while the singlet (𝑑xy,𝑑xz,𝑑yz) and triplet 𝑝-wave channels are suppressed. A unique feature of this pairing mechanism is its sensitivity to band structure and band filling.}
      \field{journaltitle}{Physical Review B}
